## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)

- es-a #12. Korean “제1、6항” and “제6호” are different citation levels. Spanish already tracks that: “apartados 1 o 6” for 항, “inciso 6” for 호. Calling both “apartado” would collapse them. The checker agrees (apartado = paragraph, inciso = item).
- es-a #18 is not a disagreement about the statute. flno=3 is article 3 of 各類所得扣繳率標準. The digit 10 stays only because the checker counts the Korean source’s 제10조. Noted under skipped.
- es-a #10 / es-b #8. The zero-width lines do pad the spoken columns. Deleting them, or turning Q16–Q20 into headings, fails the blocks/headings checks against the Korean source.
- es-a #22. The three strings are before + link label + after. Before already ends with a space. After had no leading space, so the link rendered as “Contactoexplica”. The suggested deletion assumes a leading space that was not there and would leave the words glued. A leading space was added so the line reads “la página de Contacto explica cómo…”. One space on each side of the link, not two.
- es-a #3 suggested wording replaces “recomendación” with only “recomendación de una inteligencia artificial”. That is the change round 2 rejected. The AI denial was added without dropping the general recommendation. English still denies endorsement and recommendation; “respaldo” covers endorsement.

